## Persona-v2 SQL operations

Journal schema 3 stores optional enumerated failure_code only, never native text. Preserve terminal codes through get/duplicates/restart; old terminal rows have no inferred cause. Startup interruption remains unknown, never replayable.
Journal metadata lives in a separate additive Drift database with WAL and FULL
synchronous durability. No SQL or credentials. Bootstrap/RPC/executor wiring and remaining work in
`docs/communication/sql_operations.md`. Unknown operations never reexecute.
The executor uses a dedicated connection/transaction, live policy per step/commit,
locally computed content hash, direct row limits and typed scalar outputs. Timeout
quarantines a native connection until completion; no concurrent rollback/replay.
Maintenance drains admitted operations. Initial writes target one table per step;
physical catalog proof is mandatory. sqlOperations v1 is a transport contract,
not authorization or engine certification. Advertise only with explicit
ENABLE_SQL_OPERATIONS homologation opt-in (default false); reconnect after changes.
Intersect positive limits, require durableJournal/singleSourceTransaction and
automaticReplay:false on both peers. Every handler checks negotiated capability
and the live opt-in before any journal/connection work; exceeding limits is refused,
never clamped. Preserve directlyAffectedRows:null through wire and replay storage.
Production installer/appcast gates remain blocked until full acceptance.
Coordinated persona-v2 acceptance includes shared-knowledge-and-compatibility in addition to the other gates. Removing it from a manifest cannot authorize an installer or appcast release.

## Persona SQL homologation exception

The explicitly invoked three-engine matrix under tool/homologation requires
all three private fixtures and fails on missing environment; it must never skip
or fall back to .env, configured sources or existing DSNs. This requirement
overrides optional live-test skips only for that matrix. Database identity
comes from a fixed complete metadata SELECT on the dedicated connection, not
ODBC currentCatalog. Count identity proof and row-count queries in 32 commands.
The matrix does not authorize enabling production operations or releasing builds.

## Persona-v2 source discovery

sql.describeSource v1 uses sourceDiscovery:1 negotiation and a dedicated ODBC
metadata probe in the agent, never a direct MCP connection. Require active token,
agent binding, mandatory policy database and unchanged configuration before/after.
Do not accept caller SQL or infer engine from configured driver names. DBMS metadata
must match DIALETO. Strict schemas/OpenRPC define native, provisioned and locator proofs.
SQL Anywhere locator is insufficient for durable MCP enrollment/execution.
Approved DV2-007 accepts only an explicitly DBA-provisioned UUID v4 in a version-1 marker in that
engine. Runtime never creates/repairs DBA.se7e_source_identity; technical
principal needs SELECT only on that reserved marker. Never expose it to skills.
Distinct copies require offline re-enrollment with a new UUID before binding.
Same-source restores preserve UUID and require reviewing pending operations;
a clone preserving all observed metadata is not automatically distinguishable.
expectedSource v1 plus sourceIdentity:1 negotiation bind admitted identity to the
actual business connection: verify before/after SELECT delivery and before DML
transaction begin. Never reconnect/replay verified SQL. Legacy unverified paths
are not MCP v2 fallbacks. Journal scope/content include expectedSource; duplicate
IDs never execute again. This does not replace live policy or published training.
Full live hub/agent acceptance, including DBA restore procedures, remains blocked.
See docs/communication/source_discovery.md. Keep deployment blocked.

The explicit MCP chain companion tool/homologation/persona_chain_agent_test.dart
uses production Socket.IO/RPC/ODBC, policy, Drift configuration/token metadata and
durable journals. FlutterSecure adapters use the real Windows DPAPI backend in
an exclusive temporary support directory; only directory lookup is redirected.
Never mock encryption/storage or read/migrate the operational vault. Restart
removes bootstrap secrets, recovers stable config/token identities and checks
unknown journals through RPC; never recreate business fixtures or replay SQL.
Missing/corrupt/incomplete vault refuses recovery without bootstrap fallback.
The legacy case evaluator retains its fixed empty table. The operator-only
publication companion accepts bounded typed declarations for private publication_*
tables from the session manifest, never consumer SQL. Only a fresh session may
prepare/clear them; uncertain execution requires discarding the entire fixture.
Generic cases use production hub/RPC gateways and compare complete typed results.
Never run against configured sources or in
parallel with another Flutter runner using the same native DLL. sql.execute
schema ingress must strictly accept expectedSource v1; verified materialized
responses (including chunked transport) carry explicit truncated:false only when
no truncation occurred. Preserve true upstream truncation and legacy optional
semantics on unrelated paths. Malformed profiles return typed failures. Commit
confirmation loss belongs only to the fixture, after real native commit. Desktop
bootstrap, multi-process vault concurrency, TLS/Redis and real crashes during
commit remain uncertified. Keep production opt-in blocked.

## Inspeção estrutural em desenvolvimento

O contrato `sourceSchema` v1 está em
[Communication](../../docs/communication/README.md#inspeção-estrutural-sourceschema-v1).
Manter consultas de metadados fixas por motor, recursos autorizados e prova na
conexão executora; não usar helpers genéricos como prova física dos três motores.
Nulos obrigatórios não podem ser removidos pelo saneamento do wire. Constraints
desconhecidas não viram habilitadas. SQL Anywhere 16 comprova constraints locais
por views públicas e índices físicos; FK exige configuração vigente verificável.
Escopo e limites em docs/communication/sql_operations.md.
Expectativas de constraints exigem sourceConstraints v1 e conferência na mesma
conexão antes/depois do SELECT. A extensão não libera deploy. SQL Anywhere identifica recursos BASE/VIEW regulares
por SYSTAB.table_type_str, sem classificar materialized views implicitamente. A
fixture ampla compõe 16 recursos, usa policy explícita e altera wide_07
por ações fixas do companion. A fixture rel_left/rel_link/rel_right prova FK
reversa e ponte composta N:N; outra ação fixa remove somente fk_rel_right da
base privada previamente conferida, incluindo SQL Anywhere 16 com prova vigente.
Nenhum DDL ou identificador do consumidor é aceito; a policy não libera escrita
nessas tabelas e enforcement desconhecido não habilita adoção física.

Structural SQL operations: expectedStructure requires expectedSource plus exact
sqlOperations.structureGuard:1/sourceSchema/sourceIdentity negotiation and
sourceConstraints v1 for keys. Metadata read authorization and same-connection
checks before transaction begin are mandatory; all fixed metadata statements
consume the 32-command budget. No fallback on old peers. Contract and pending
hub/MCP integration: docs/communication/sql_operations.md. Release stays blocked.

Transactional sql.operation.execute requires exact resource names and bypasses legacy decision-cache reads/writes. Quote native namespace segments separately where supported; Firebird remains schema-less. No automatic snapshot/grant conversion. Contract: docs/communication/sql_operations.md.

Managed pagination must order by verified output names. A qualified inner column
requires an exact simple projection mapping, used for both wrapper SQL and cursor
lookup; missing/ambiguous mappings fail closed. MCP/hub do not rewrite business
SQL. Contract and narrow grammar: docs/communication/sql_operations.md.
